    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Brice Turang** stands as the clear anchor of our lineup with a 65.44 efficiency score. While we are awaiting the official lineup card, his assumed promotion to the #2 spot, paired with a favorable matchup against the Roki Sasaki delivery profile, makes him a primary source of our target category, stolen bases. The model aggressively weights his speed against the SP\u2019s slower delivery, which provides a significant boost to his floor. Conversely, **Travis Bazzana** (56.66) represents a strong, high-upside play against Montero, benefiting from a +10% SP skill adjustment and a favorable platoon setup that allows him to outperform his base projection despite hitting toward the bottom of the order.\n\nNavigating the remainder of the roster requires balancing marginal projections against the scarcity of our speed categories. **Josh Naylor** (54.97) and **Seiya Suzuki** (52.65) are relegated to \"marginal\" starts due to challenging matchups against Fried and Cavalli, respectively. While **Seiya Suzuki** retains some value due to his prime batting position, the high xERA of these opposing arms suppresses his ceiling. **Jose Caballero** (44.60) is the weakest link in today\u2019s starting five; he is essentially a roster filler dictated by our need to avoid burning caps while maintaining stolen base exposure. Given that our high-upside assets like **Corbin Carroll** are sidelined due to the schedule and **James Wood** remains on the IL, we are effectively playing a \"defensive\" rotation to maximize efficiency over raw volume. \n\nThe most difficult bench decision was determining how to handle the lower-tier utility spots, specifically weighing the potential output of players like **Zach McKinstry** or **Tyler Soderstrom** against the established, albeit marginal, value of **Jose Caballero**. Ultimately, the proximity of the scores meant the optimizer favored the structural consistency of our current lineup, opting to keep **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** on the bench to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable pitching conditions later in the week. We continue to monitor the status of **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story**, but with no game action for them today, our primary concern remains navigating the elite arms we are currently facing.",
